body:
`.body` can shrink to zero (`min-height: 0`), but its content cannot: the closed groups are `flex: none`, `.groupWhat` is `flex: none`, and `.rows` keeps a 72px floor. Take a window near the 560px minimum (`BASE_MIN_HEIGHT`) with all four groups present. By my estimate (not checked in a browser), the fixed heights come to roughly 560px, while the dialog gets about 510px. `.body` keeps overflow visible, so the list draws over the summary line and the Fix button instead of being contained. Scrolling `.body` as a fallback keeps the footer clear. When everything fits, nothing scrolls there, so the one-scroll design is unchanged.

```suggestion
.body {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-height: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-sm);
  /* Fallback for very short windows: the footer stays clear when even the minimum list does not fit. */
  overflow-y: auto;
}
```
